  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/l134-peckoltia-compta-2/",
      "html": "<p>P. compta is one of the most recommendable L-catfishes and combines all desired characteristics of this group in an ideal way: small size (maximum 12 cm with tail fin), splendid coloring, a little shy nature and comparatively easy breeding.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/l134-peckoltia-compta-2/",
      "html": "<p>L134 (Peckoltia compta) comes from the Rio Tapajós.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/10-catfishes/l134-peckoltia-compta-2/",
      "html": "<p>Distinguishing the sexes is tricky and often ends unsatisfactorily for the aquarist. Although sexually active males are always easy to recognize, boyish females are not, and males that are ranked far below cannot be distinguished from females at all.</p>"
    }
  ],
